{"s":58,"v":[{"t":"Certainly has Allāh heard the speech of the one who argues [i.e., pleads] with you, [O Muḥammad], concerning her husband and directs her complaint to Allāh. And Allāh hears your dialogue; indeed, Allāh is Hearing and Seeing.","w":[["قَدْ","Indeed","qad",""],["سَمِعَ","Allah has heard","samiʿa",""],["ٱللَّهُ","Allah has heard","l-lahu",""],["قَوْلَ","(the) speech","qawla",""],["ٱلَّتِى","(of one) who","allatī",""],["تُجَـٰدِلُكَ","disputes with you","tujādiluka","",[["تُجَـٰدِلُ",431],["كَ",18]]],["فِى","concerning","fī",""],["زَوْجِهَا","her husband","zawjihā","",[["زَوْجِ",165],["هَا",22]]],["وَتَشْتَكِىٓ","and she directs her complaint","watashtakī","",[["وَ",1],["تَشْتَكِىٓ",3186]]],["إِلَى","to","ilā",""],["ٱللَّهِ","Allah","l-lahi",""],["وَٱللَّهُ","And Allah","wal-lahu","",[["وَ",1],["ٱللَّهُ",9]]],["يَسْمَعُ","hears","yasmaʿu",""],["تَحَاوُرَكُمَآ","(the) dialogue of both of you","taḥāwurakumā","ۚ",[["تَحَاوُرَ",3136],["كُمَآ",110]]],["إِنَّ","Indeed","inna",""],["ٱللَّهَ","Allah","l-laha",""],["سَمِيعٌۢ","(is) All-Hearer","samīʿun",""],["بَصِيرٌ","All-Seer","baṣīrun",""]]},{"t":"Those who pronounce ẓihār among you [to separate] from their wives - they are not [consequently] their mothers. Their mothers are none but those who gave birth to them. And indeed, they are saying an objectionable statement and a falsehood. But indeed, Allāh is Pardoning and Forgiving.","w":[["ٱلَّذِينَ","Those who","alladhīna",""],["يُظَـٰهِرُونَ","pronounce zihar","yuẓāhirūna","",[["يُظَـٰهِرُ",1183],["ونَ",3]]],["مِنكُم","among you","minkum","",[["مِن",6],["كُم",4]]],["مِّن","[from]","min",""],["نِّسَآئِهِم","(to) their wives","nisāihim","",[["نِّسَآئِ",210],["هِم",3]]],["مَّا","not","mā",""],["هُنَّ","they","hunna",""],["أُمَّهَـٰتِهِمْ","(are) their mothers","ummahātihim","ۖ",[["أُمَّهَـٰتِ",336],["هِمْ",3]]],["إِنْ","Not","in",""],["أُمَّهَـٰتُهُمْ","(are) their mothers","ummahātuhum","",[["أُمَّهَـٰتُ",336],["هُمْ",3]]],["إِلَّا","except","illā",""],["ٱلَّـٰٓـِٔى","those who","allāī",""],["وَلَدْنَهُمْ","gave them birth","waladnahum","ۚ",[["وَلَدْ",933],["نَ",52],["هُمْ",3]]],["وَإِنَّهُمْ","And indeed, they","wa-innahum","",[["وَ",1],["إِنَّ",15],["هُمْ",3]]],["لَيَقُولُونَ","surely say","layaqūlūna","",[["لَ",23],["يَقُولُ",16],["ونَ",3]]],["مُنكَرًۭا","an evil","munkaran",""],["مِّنَ","[of]","mina",""],["ٱلْقَوْلِ","[the] word","l-qawli","",[["ٱلْ",2],["قَوْلِ",137]]],["وَزُورًۭا","and a lie","wazūran","ۚ",[["وَ",1],["زُورًۭا",1534]]],["وَإِنَّ","But indeed","wa-inna","",[["وَ",1],["إِنَّ",15]]],["ٱللَّهَ","Allah","l-laha",""],["لَعَفُوٌّ","(is) surely, Oft-Pardoning","laʿafuwwun","",[["لَ",23],["عَفُوٌّ",1368]]],["غَفُورٌۭ","Oft-Forgiving","ghafūrun",""]]},{"t":"And those who pronounce ẓihār from their wives and then [wish to] go back on what they said - then [there must be] the freeing of a slave before they touch one another. That is what you are admonished thereby; and Allāh is Aware of what you do.","w":[["وَٱلَّذِينَ","And those who","wa-alladhīna","",[["وَ",1],["ٱلَّذِينَ",17]]],["يُظَـٰهِرُونَ","pronounce zihar","yuẓāhirūna","",[["يُظَـٰهِرُ",1183],["ونَ",3]]],["مِن","[from]","min",""],["نِّسَآئِهِمْ","(to) their wives","nisāihim","",[["نِّسَآئِ",210],["هِمْ",3]]],["ثُمَّ","then","thumma",""],["يَعُودُونَ","go back","yaʿūdūna","",[["يَعُودُ",549],["ونَ",3]]],["لِمَا","on what","limā","",[["لِ",8],["مَا",12]]],["قَالُوا۟","they said","qālū","",[["قَالُ",16],["وا۟",3]]],["فَتَحْرِيرُ","then freeing","fataḥrīru","",[["فَ",7],["تَحْرِيرُ",1292]]],["رَقَبَةٍۢ","(of) a slave","raqabatin",""],["مِّن","before","min",""],["قَبْلِ","before","qabli",""],["أَن","[that]","an",""],["يَتَمَآسَّا","they touch each other","yatamāssā","ۚ",[["يَتَمَآسَّ",2769],["ا",66]]],["ذَٰلِكُمْ","That","dhālikum","",[["ذَٰ",32],["لِ",0],["كُمْ",0]]],["تُوعَظُونَ","you are admonished","tūʿaẓūna","",[["تُوعَظُ",636],["ونَ",4]]],["بِهِۦ","to it","bihi","ۚ",[["بِ",10],["هِۦ",5]]],["وَٱللَّهُ","And Allah","wal-lahu","",[["وَ",1],["ٱللَّهُ",9]]],["بِمَا","of what","bimā","",[["بِ",10],["مَا",12]]],["تَعْمَلُونَ","you do","taʿmalūna","",[["تَعْمَلُ",58],["ونَ",4]]],["خَبِيرٌۭ","(is) All-Aware","khabīrun",""]]},{"t":"And he who does not find [a slave] - then a fast for two months consecutively before they touch one another; and he who is unable - then the feeding of sixty poor persons. That is for you to believe [completely] in Allāh and His Messenger; and those are the limits [set by] Allāh. And for the disbelievers is a painful punishment.","w":[["فَمَن","Then whoever","faman","",[["فَ",7],["مَن",25]]],["لَّمْ","(does) not","lam",""],["يَجِدْ","find","yajid",""],["فَصِيَامُ","then fasting","faṣiyāmu","",[["فَ",7],["صِيَامُ",901]]],["شَهْرَيْنِ","(for) two months","shahrayni",""],["مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ","consecutively","mutatābiʿayni",""],["مِن","before","min",""],["قَبْلِ","before","qabli",""],["أَن","[that]","an",""],["يَتَمَآسَّا","they both touch each other","yatamāssā","ۖ",[["يَتَمَآسَّ",2769],["ا",66]]],["فَمَن","But (he) who","faman","",[["فَ",7],["مَن",25]]],["لَّمْ","not","lam",""],["يَسْتَطِعْ","is able","yastaṭiʿ",""],["فَإِطْعَامُ","then (the) feeding","fa-iṭ'ʿāmu","",[["فَ",7],["إِطْعَامُ",1732]]],["سِتِّينَ","(of) sixty","sittīna",""],["مِسْكِينًۭا","needy one(s)","mis'kīnan","ۚ"],["ذَٰلِكَ","That ","dhālika","",[["ذَٰ",32],["لِ",0],["كَ",0]]],["لِتُؤْمِنُوا۟","so that you may believe","litu'minū","",[["لِ",8],["تُؤْمِنُ",30],["وا۟",4]]],["بِٱللَّهِ","in Allah","bil-lahi","",[["بِ",10],["ٱللَّهِ",9]]],["وَرَسُولِهِۦ","and His Messenger","warasūlihi","ۚ",[["وَ",1],["رَسُولِ",47],["هِۦ",5]]],["وَتِلْكَ","and these","watil'ka","",[["وَ",1],["تِ",279],["لْ",0],["كَ",0]]],["حُدُودُ","(are the) limits","ḥudūdu",""],["ٱللَّهِ","(of) Allah","l-lahi","ۗ"],["وَلِلْكَـٰفِرِينَ","and for the disbelievers","walil'kāfirīna","",[["وَ",1],["لِ",8],["لْ",2],["كَـٰفِرِينَ",88]]],["عَذَابٌ","(is) a punishment","ʿadhābun",""],["أَلِيمٌ","painful","alīmun",""]]},{"t":"Indeed, those who oppose Allāh and His Messenger are abased as those before them were abased. And We have certainly sent down verses of clear evidence. And for the disbelievers is a humiliating punishment","w":[["إِنَّ","Indeed","inna",""],["ٱلَّذِينَ","those who","alladhīna",""],["يُحَآدُّونَ","oppose","yuḥāddūna","",[["يُحَآدُّ",2803],["ونَ",3]]],["ٱللَّهَ","Allah","l-laha",""],["وَرَسُولَهُۥ","and His Messenger","warasūlahu","",[["وَ",1],["رَسُولَ",47],["هُۥ",5]]],["كُبِتُوا۟","(will) be disgraced","kubitū","",[["كُبِتُ",1959],["وا۟",3]]],["كَمَا","as","kamā","",[["كَ",54],["مَا",12]]],["كُبِتَ","were disgraced","kubita",""],["ٱلَّذِينَ","those","alladhīna",""],["مِن","before them","min",""],["قَبْلِهِمْ","before them","qablihim","ۚ",[["قَبْلِ",65],["هِمْ",3]]],["وَقَدْ","And certainly","waqad","",[["وَ",1],["قَدْ",37]]],["أَنزَلْنَآ","We have sent down","anzalnā","",[["أَنزَلْ",77],["نَآ",11]]],["ءَايَـٰتٍۭ","Verses","āyātin",""],["بَيِّنَـٰتٍۢ","clear","bayyinātin","ۚ"],["وَلِلْكَـٰفِرِينَ","And for the disbelievers","walil'kāfirīna","",[["وَ",1],["لِ",8],["لْ",2],["كَـٰفِرِينَ",88]]],["عَذَابٌۭ","(is) a punishment","ʿadhābun",""],["مُّهِينٌۭ","humiliating","muhīnun",""]]},{"t":"On the Day when Allāh will resurrect them all and inform them of what they did. Allāh had enumerated it, while they forgot it; and Allāh is, over all things, Witness.","w":[["يَوْمَ","(On the) Day","yawma",""],["يَبْعَثُهُمُ","(when) Allah will raise them","yabʿathuhumu","",[["يَبْعَثُ",235],["هُمُ",3]]],["ٱللَّهُ","(when) Allah will raise them","l-lahu",""],["جَمِيعًۭا","all","jamīʿan",""],["فَيُنَبِّئُهُم","and inform them","fayunabbi-uhum","",[["فَ",7],["يُنَبِّئُ",265],["هُم",3]]],["بِمَا","of what","bimā","",[["بِ",10],["مَا",12]]],["عَمِلُوٓا۟","they did","ʿamilū","ۚ",[["عَمِلُ",58],["وٓا۟",3]]],["أَحْصَىٰهُ","Allah has recorded it","aḥṣāhu","",[["أَحْصَىٰ",806],["هُ",5]]],["ٱللَّهُ","Allah has recorded it","l-lahu",""],["وَنَسُوهُ","while they forgot it","wanasūhu","ۚ",[["وَ",1],["نَسُ",346],["و",3],["هُ",5]]],["وَٱللَّهُ","And Allah","wal-lahu","",[["وَ",1],["ٱللَّهُ",9]]],["عَلَىٰ","(is) over","ʿalā",""],["كُلِّ","all","kulli",""],["شَىْءٍۢ","things","shayin",""],["شَهِيدٌ","a Witness","shahīdun",""]]},{"t":"Have you not considered that Allāh knows what is in the heavens and what is on the earth? There are not three in a private conversation but that He is the fourth of them, nor are there five but that He is the sixth of them - and no less than that and no more except that He is with them [in knowledge] wherever they are. Then He will inform them of what they did, on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed Allāh is, of all things, Knowing.","w":[["أَلَمْ","Do not","alam","",[["أَ",31],["لَمْ",44]]],["تَرَ","you see","tara",""],["أَنَّ","that","anna",""],["ٱللَّهَ","Allah","l-laha",""],["يَعْلَمُ","knows","yaʿlamu",""],["مَا","whatever","mā",""],["فِى","(is) in","fī",""],["ٱلسَّمَـٰوَٰتِ","the heavens","l-samāwāti","",[["ٱل",2],["سَّمَـٰوَٰتِ",49]]],["وَمَا","and whatever","wamā","",[["وَ",1],["مَا",12]]],["فِى","(is) in","fī",""],["ٱلْأَرْضِ","the earth","l-arḍi","ۖ",[["ٱلْ",2],["أَرْضِ",35]]],["مَا","Not","mā",""],["يَكُونُ","there is","yakūnu",""],["مِن","any","min",""],["نَّجْوَىٰ","secret counsel","najwā",""],["ثَلَـٰثَةٍ","(of) three","thalāthatin",""],["إِلَّا","but","illā",""],["هُوَ","He (is)","huwa",""],["رَابِعُهُمْ","(the) fourth of them","rābiʿuhum","",[["رَابِعُ",2373],["هُمْ",3]]],["وَلَا","and not","walā","",[["وَ",1],["لَا",13]]],["خَمْسَةٍ","five","khamsatin",""],["إِلَّا","but","illā",""],["هُوَ","He (is)","huwa",""],["سَادِسُهُمْ","(the) sixth of them","sādisuhum","",[["سَادِسُ",2409],["هُمْ",3]]],["وَلَآ","and not","walā","",[["وَ",1],["لَآ",13]]],["أَدْنَىٰ","less","adnā",""],["مِن","than","min",""],["ذَٰلِكَ","that","dhālika","",[["ذَٰ",32],["لِ",0],["كَ",0]]],["وَلَآ","and not","walā","",[["وَ",1],["لَآ",13]]],["أَكْثَرَ","more","akthara",""],["إِلَّا","but","illā",""],["هُوَ","He","huwa",""],["مَعَهُمْ","(is) with them","maʿahum","",[["مَعَ",84],["هُمْ",3]]],["أَيْنَ","wherever","ayna",""],["مَا","wherever","mā",""],["كَانُوا۟","they are","kānū","ۖ",[["كَانُ",21],["وا۟",3]]],["ثُمَّ","Then","thumma",""],["يُنَبِّئُهُم","He will inform them","yunabbi-uhum","",[["يُنَبِّئُ",265],["هُم",3]]],["بِمَا","of what","bimā","",[["بِ",10],["مَا",12]]],["عَمِلُوا۟","they did","ʿamilū","",[["عَمِلُ",58],["وا۟",3]]],["يَوْمَ","(on the) Day","yawma",""],["ٱلْقِيَـٰمَةِ","(of) the Resurrection","l-qiyāmati","ۚ",[["ٱلْ",2],["قِيَـٰمَةِ",187]]],["إِنَّ","Indeed","inna",""],["ٱللَّهَ","Allah","l-laha",""],["بِكُلِّ","of every","bikulli","",[["بِ",10],["كُلِّ",43]]],["شَىْءٍ","thing","shayin",""],["عَلِيمٌ","(is) All-Knower","ʿalīmun",""]]},{"t":"Have you not considered those who were forbidden from private conversation [i.e., ridicule and conspiracy] and then return to that which they were forbidden and converse among themselves about sin and aggression and disobedience to the Messenger? And when they come to you, they greet you with that [word] by which Allāh does not greet you and say among themselves, \"Why does Allāh not punish us for what we say?\" Sufficient for them is Hell, which they will [enter to] burn, and wretched is the destination.","w":[["أَلَمْ","Do not","alam","",[["أَ",31],["لَمْ",44]]],["تَرَ","you see","tara",""],["إِلَى","[to]","ilā",""],["ٱلَّذِينَ","those who","alladhīna",""],["نُهُوا۟","were forbidden","nuhū","",[["نُهُ",367],["وا۟",3]]],["عَنِ","from","ʿani",""],["ٱلنَّجْوَىٰ","secret counsels","l-najwā","",[["ٱل",2],["نَّجْوَىٰ",795]]],["ثُمَّ","then","thumma",""],["يَعُودُونَ","they return","yaʿūdūna","",[["يَعُودُ",549],["ونَ",3]]],["لِمَا","to what","limā","",[["لِ",8],["مَا",12]]],["نُهُوا۟","they were forbidden","nuhū","",[["نُهُ",367],["وا۟",3]]],["عَنْهُ","from [it]","ʿanhu","",[["عَنْ",34],["هُ",5]]],["وَيَتَنَـٰجَوْنَ","and they hold secret counsels","wayatanājawna","",[["وَ",1],["يَتَنَـٰجَ",1499],["وْنَ",3]]],["بِٱلْإِثْمِ","for sin","bil-ith'mi","",[["بِ",10],["ٱلْ",2],["إِثْمِ",337]]],["وَٱلْع